    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't even recognize myself in the mirror anymore. everything i was... the strength, the way i moved... it’s just gone. my body feels like this heavy, broken thing that i’m just forced to carry around. it's like the person i actually was died when the injury happened, and now i'm just a shell.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It takes immense courage to feel this deeply about your identity, and your grief for \"who you were before\" is completely valid given what you've been through. While painful, it's important to remember that healing isn't just physical but that your inner strength hasn't vanished, even if the mirror reflects a struggle right now. Giving yourself permission to take it one small step at a time, perhaps with a therapist or a supportive friend, can help reconnect the person inside you with the person outside.",
